# Byte-faithful historical probe source (not a dataset payload)
!**/evidence/phase0/raw/
!**/evidence/phase0/raw/SHA256SUMS
# Directory placeholders. The object stores are intentionally empty in the handoff
# (the payloads are inventoried in DATASETS.local.json), but `cargo run -p xtask -- audit`
# requires the directories to EXIST. Without these two negations the `**/objects/` rule
# strips the placeholders, the directories vanish from a clone, and the audit hard-fails
# for all 29 modules with "object or movement directory is absent".
!**/evidence/phase0/raw/objects/
!**/evidence/phase0/raw/objects/.gitkeep
!**/evidence/phase0/split/
!**/evidence/phase0/split/split-manifest.v1.json
!**/evidence/superseded/
!**/evidence/superseded/**
!amphora-ip-fto-guard/evidence/audit/kpi-recompute-consistency-v1/raw/
!amphora-ip-fto-guard/evidence/audit/kpi-recompute-consistency-v1/raw/*.Cargo.toml
!amphora-ip-fto-guard/evidence/audit/kpi-recompute-consistency-v1/raw/*.rs

# Inventoried payloads that no pattern above covers.
#
# Every path in DATASETS.local.json is deliberately outside Git. Most are caught by the
# bulk rules (**/raw/, **/derived/, **/objects/, **/splits/, **/quarantine/), but these
# five are not: two sit under an ip-fto-guard `raw/` directory that is explicitly negated
# above so its .rs/.Cargo.toml probe sources stay tracked, and three sit at paths the bulk
# rules never matched.
#
# Without these lines a completed `ops/restore-datasets.sh` leaves `git status` dirty and
# `git add -A` would stage rights-unresolved data. The publication policy would still
# refuse it, but the boundary should hold at the earliest gate, not the last one.
/amphora-ip-fto-guard/evidence/audit/kpi-recompute-consistency-v1/raw/probe.output1.json
/amphora-ip-fto-guard/evidence/audit/kpi-recompute-consistency-v1/raw/probe.output2.json
/amphora-known-answer-benchmarks/evidence/phase0/repairs/R-A05/work/a702b75_us_tds.pdf
/amphora-optimizer-orchestrator/evidence/audit/optimizer-authorization-numeric-comparison-conformance-v1/runtime_ground_truth.v1.jsonl
/amphora-optimizer-orchestrator/evidence/audit/optimizer-constraint-path-addressing-grammar-v1/runtime_ground_truth.v1.jsonl

# Host-local trees, on a consolidated handoff host.
#
# The handoff host keeps one directory. These two live inside it and are deliberately
# outside Git:
#
#   state/   the controller's mutable state -- HARD_STOP, campaign.json, the acquisition
#            queue, locks, counters, logs. The controller separates code from state on
#            purpose; this is the state half, and it is host-specific.
#   legacy/  archives kept for provenance: the lossless pre-split controller archive
#            (which holds commit 8d76070, cited by directives/CORRECTIONS.md) and the
#            dated loop-operations reports from when the fleet was running.
#
# WARNING: `git clean -xdf` removes ignored files, so it would delete both of these AND
# the ~6.2 GB restored dataset inventory. On a host that cannot reach the canonical tree,
# that data is not recoverable locally. Do not run it here.
/state/
/legacy/

